Local patch to Arnis (https://github.com/louis-e/arnis, Apache License 2.0, Copyright (c) 2022-2026
Louis Erbkamm), applied to the source at ARNIS_REF by .github/workflows/build.yml before `cargo build`.
It changes src/elevation/mod.rs and src/elevation/postprocess.rs; both carry a "Local change" comment.

What it adds: an elevation base grid. With ARNIS_ELEVATION_BASE_M=<metres> in the environment, the ordinary
fit (AffinePolicy::Fit) becomes AffinePolicy::Grid: heights are mapped at ARNIS_ELEVATION_SCALE (times
--height-multiplier; the run's own vertical scale when unset) blocks per metre, from a base a whole number of
blocks above <metres> (the bbox's lowest cell, rounded down onto that grid), instead of from the bbox's own
lowest cell. Two bakes of neighbouring bboxes then give one ground point the same height up to a whole number
of blocks. A bbox whose relief does not fit the build height at that scale falls back to the ordinary fit
(and says so). Without the variable nothing changes; One World runs (FitWithHeadroom/Fixed) are untouched,
and --lidar works as before. build.py sets the variables for areas with "elevation_base_m".

